<title>UK: AHB adds 500 million marks to five-year bond.</title>
<headline>AHB adds 500 million marks to five-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allgemeine Hypothekenbank has issued a 500 million mark tranche of its 5.00 percent December 2001 bond priced at 99.94, Dresdner Bank said as one of five joint lead managers.</p>
<p>The total size is now 2.0 billion marks.  </p>
<p>The other joint leads are Commerzbank, Deutsche Morgan Grenfell, DG Bank and Helaba.</p>
<p>+ + +</p>
<p> AMT   *500 MLN DEM   COUPON     5.00	MATURITY    03.DEC.01</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.94     PAY DATE    15.NOV.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.25	LISTING    FRANKFURT PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.06	SELL CONC  0.02	DENOMS (K)  1</p>
<p> NOTES     *LAUNCHED 02.OCT AS A 1.5 BLN DEM DEAL AT 99.45</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
